WEBVTT

00:02:59.844 --> 00:03:01.356
After the Opium Wars,

00:03:01.356 --> 00:03:03.560
Chinese breeds were brought to England

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.720
and crossed with local chickens.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.728
This gave rise to a phenomenon called

00:03:07.728 --> 00:03:09.225
“Hen Fever”

00:03:09.225 --> 00:03:10.634
or “The Fancy”,

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:12.194
with farmers all over Europe

00:03:12.194 --> 00:03:14.311
striving to breed new varieties

00:03:14.311 --> 00:03:17.105
with particular combinations of traits.

00:03:17.105 --> 00:03:19.053
This trend also caught the attention

00:03:19.053 --> 00:03:21.373
of a certain Charles Darwin,
who wondered if

00:03:21.373 --> 00:03:25.291
a similar selective breeding process
occurred in nature.

00:03:25.291 --> 00:03:27.930
Darwin would observe hundreds of chickens

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.147
while finalizing his historic work